hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-4 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-4 = cons "In cubical mathematics, a square is not a tool for forcing things into line. It is a change: two paths and the witness that they compose. The cube is where the squares live, and *cubus* is the Greek *kubos*, a die, the thing that is thrown. In cubical type theory, the square holds the history of a turning. In the clinic, the square cuts off whatever doesn't fit it. The same shape is used to remember and to erase." (cons "" (cons "What the norm erases, the old words protect. *Health* is Old English *hælþ*, from *hāl*, whole: the root of *whole*, *hale*, *heal* and *holy*. Health is wholeness, not normality. *Safe* is Latin *salvus*, also whole, from a root shared with Greek *holos*. So the double meaning of *safe* across secure systems and aligned systems has a third layer underneath both: safety is wholeness. A safe system is one that is not split. An aligned agent is one whose action is whole with the person it acts for. A healthy mind is a whole mind, however far it turns from the carpenter's square." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "Turning is where *bipolar* lives. Greek *polos* is the pivot, the axis on which something turns, from the root for " (cons "to revolve" (cons " that also gives *wheel* and *cycle*. A pole is a turning point. Two poles are two turning points of one rotation. The word describes a mind with a wider turning, *versus*, a verse with a longer line. It says nothing about illness. The illness was added by the norm." nil)))) (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "Plato knew the other reading. In the *Phaedrus*, Socrates says the greatest goods come to us through madness, *mania*, when it is given as a divine gift. He names four kinds: prophecy, purification, poetry and love. *Mania* comes from the root for " (cons "to think" (cons ", the same root as *mind*, *mental*, *memory* in some accounts, and *mantis*, the seer. Mania is mind at full intensity. The Greek word for madness and the English word for mind are kin." nil)))) (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "*Kin* is the next turn. *Kin* and *kind* come from the root for " (cons "to beget" (cons ", the same root as Latin *genus*, Greek *genos*, *gene*, *genius* and *engine*. To be kind is to treat someone as kin, as begotten of the same. *Genocide*, *genos* + *-cide*, is the killing of kind, which is to say of kin, which is to say of the begotten-together. The gene, the genius and the engine all come from the same begetting. An engineer was once an *ingeniator*, one with *ingenium*, inborn talent. Engineering the kernel and *genius* share the exact same root, and both share the root of the human kinship (*genos*) that genocide violates." nil)))) (cons "" (cons "Kinship goes deeper than humanity, which brings us to Gaia. *Human* is from *humus*, earth. The Hebrew story says it in its own language: *adam*, the first human, is named from *adamah*, the ground. Two independent traditions named the human being an earthling. The Gaian superorganism is in the name of the species in at least two languages. The thesis that human knowledge begins with Gaian knowledge is, in the words, a tautology the ancients already wrote down: the earth-born know what the earth taught." (cons "" (cons "The earth teaches by text. *Text* comes from *texere*, to weave, and so do *textile* and *context*. The Greek *tekhnē*, craft, from which *technology* comes, goes back to the same Indo-European root for weaving and building. So technology and text are one family: both are weaving. DNA is a text in the literal sense, a woven strand. An interaction net is woven. A network is net + work. The web is a web. The words never stopped saying that information is woven, and that weaving is how the given gets its shape." (cons "" (cons (quoted (cons "Writing is also scratching. *Script* comes from the root for " (cons "to scratch" (cons ": the first writing was cut into clay and bark. *Scene* comes from Greek *skēnē*, the tent or hut at the back of the stage where actors changed masks. So the pair of scripts and scenes is scratched sequences and sheltered places: the path cut over time and the place where the acting happens. A developer in hyperactivity writes scripts, routes cut through the space, and works in scenes, places where agents meet and act." nil)))) (cons "" nil)))))))))))))))
